-- Fair Trading Act 1986 — TESTS.
-- Expected values are worked from
-- ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_121.txt, not from the code.
-- The working-day calendar is made up: 25 and 26 December 2025 and 1 and 2
-- January 2026 are taken as non-working weekdays.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

`the calendar` MEANS `Working day calendar` OF LIST Date 25 12 2025, Date 26 12 2025, Date 1 1 2026, Date 2 1 2026

-- Conduct engaging p, with its quality, in trade or not, by a person of a
-- kind; not the Crown, no news media, no clause, loss discovered 1 March 2025.
GIVEN p IS A Prohibition, quality IS A BOOLEAN, trade IS A BOOLEAN, kind IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A `Conduct case`
`conduct` p quality trade kind MEANS
    `Conduct case` OF p, quality, trade, kind, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, Date 1 3 2025

`a valid clause` MEANS `Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

`misleading in trade` MEANS `conduct` `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade` TRUE TRUE `a body corporate`

GIVEN who IS A `Who cancelled the layby`, provides IS A BOOLEAN, breach IS A BOOLEAN, claimed IS A NUMBER, costs IS A NUMBER, paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Layby cancellation`
`layby cancelled by` who provides breach claimed costs paid MEANS
    `Layby cancellation` OF who, provides, breach, claimed, costs, paid

